    "lawCode": "Add §343-aa, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3550A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to\ndesignating a portion of state highway in Erie county as the \"Sergeant\nWilliam R. Wilson III Memorial Highway\"\n\nPURPOSE: To designate a portion of the interstate highway 990 as the\n\"Sergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSUMMARY: Section 1 amends the highway law by adding a new section,\n343-aa in order that a portion of interstate highway 990 be designated\nas the \"Sergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2 directs the commissioner of the department of transportation\nto provide for \"Sergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway\"\nsignage and provides that the name designation shall be one of a\nceremonial nature.\n\nSection 3 provides the enacting clause.\n\nJUSTIFICATION: This legislation would celebrate the late US Army Sgt.\nWilliam R. Wilson III, of Getzville, in Erie County, who was killed\nMarch 26, 2012, while serving in Afghanistan. Sergeant Wilson was\nkilled in Paktika Province, in Eastern Afghanistan, where he was\ntraining Afghan soldiers and police to take over the country's\nsecurity when the United States withdraws from Afghanistan in 2014.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None. Current project costs will cover the\nsignage.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
