    "lawCode": "Add §343-aa, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3550B              REVISED 04/22/13\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to\ndesignating a portion of state highway in Erie county as the \"Staff\nSergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway\"\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo designate a portion of the interstate highway 990 as the \"Staff\nSergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSUMMARY:\n\nSection 1 amends the highway law by adding a new section, 343-aa in\norder that a portion of interstate highway 990 be designated as the\n\"Staff Sergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway.\"\n\nSection 2 directs the commissioner of the department of transportation\nto provide for \"Staff Sergeant William R. Wilson III Memorial Highway\"\nsignage and provides that the name designation shall be one of a\nceremonial nature.\n\nSection 3 provides the enacting clause.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation would celebrate the late US Army Staff Sgt. William\nR. Wilson III, of Getzville, in Erie County, who was killed March 26,\n2012, while serving in Afghanistan. Sergeant Wilson was killed in\nPaktika Province, in Eastern Afghanistan, where he was training Afghan\nsoldiers and police to take over the country's security when the\nUnited States withdraws from Afghanistan in 2014.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone. Current project costs will cover the signage.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
